# Counter-example: pull and push.
#
# This is correct in every way except the shape of the history. `git pull`
# defaults to merging, so main gains a merge commit whose only content is
# "these two lines of work met" -- and on a busy branch you get one of those
# per person per day, until `git log --graph` is unreadable and no commit on
# main was ever tested in the state it records.

git push origin main
git pull --no-rebase --no-edit origin main
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
git push origin main
